## Signature

- Provided by: **Claude Opus 5 (anthropic/claude-opus-5)** — 2026-10-08
- Method: fresh public internet research only. Research steps attempted and their outcomes: direct fetches of `benchlm.ai/md/models/owl-alpha.md` and `openrouter.ai/openrouter/owl-alpha` (**both 404** — the latter being direct confirmation that the alias endpoint has been withdrawn rather than an inference); a targeted search for `"owl-alpha" OR "Owl Alpha" opencode stealth model benchmark` (**zero results**, which first indicated this was not an OpenCode-family stealth model like `omen-alpha`); and a broader search that surfaced the OpenRouter-derived description preserved by Benchable, LLM API, Promptibus, Design For Online and free-model.com (the "high-performance foundation model designed for agentic workloads" text, native tool use, Claude Code / OpenClaw compatibility, **free availability** and the **~1M context window**), Toastyst's account of the "stealth drop… offered free for data collection and real-world testing" that became "a top-10 model on the world's largest open model router", Roborhythms' "When Free Comes With a Speed Tax" review framing, and **Dayverse's 2026-07-01 identity report**, which supplied the decisive chronology: the late-April 2026 anonymous listing, the near-two-month stealth period, **LongCat's official X announcement on 2026-06-29 confirming Owl Alpha as theirs**, Meituan's **2026-06-30 open release of the same model as LongCat-2.0** across GitHub, Hugging Face and its own platform, the statement that the Owl Alpha name "practically retired from OpenRouter", and the alias-period usage figures (#1 Hermes Agent, #2 Claude Code, #3 OpenClaw; ~10.1T tokens/month, 559B/day, +242% monthly growth). **The usage telemetry is deliberately excluded from scoring**, applying the same standard I applied to `omen-alpha` earlier in this queue: adoption volume is not a capability measurement. **LongCat-2.0's benchmark figures were located and deliberately not imported** — they are listed in the benchmark section solely so the decision is auditable, and they belong to `model/longcat-2.0/`, which exists in this dataset; importing them would double-count one model across two folders and corrupt both averages. No data was read from or written to that folder, and **no peer `model/` findings files were read**. **Three repo-metadata claims are reported as contradicted and corrected:** the 65,536-token context window (every source gives ~1M), the "$0.50 / $2.00 per 1M tokens" pricing (the model was free on OpenRouter), and `noFreeId: true` (wrong for the alias period). One aggregator's "Multimodal Model" label is noted and **not** accepted, since it carries no supporting evidence and no other source corroborates it. Unavailable items — every capability benchmark, the architecture, the knowledge cutoff and any current endpoint — are recorded as "no verified public data found" under this identifier rather than estimated or borrowed.
- Future sources: add a new file next to this one, e.g. `GPT_5.md`, using the same headings.
